1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:06,372
Look, the stars are blinking like little trembling lamps…

2
00:00:06,422 --> 00:00:08,432
and that one, right at the horizon,

3
00:00:08,482 --> 00:00:09,433
dances even more!

4
00:00:09,483 --> 00:00:10,954
But why do stars twinkle?

5
00:00:11,785 --> 00:00:13,191
But Mila sees a very bright

6
00:00:13,241 --> 00:00:14,915
dot that doesn't tremble at all.

7
00:00:14,965 --> 00:00:15,562
Noah checks…

8
00:00:15,612 --> 00:00:16,317
it's a planet!

9
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:17,714
Why does it stay so calm?

10
00:00:18,482 --> 00:00:19,996
Discovery mission!

11
00:00:22,512 --> 00:00:23,043
Mini mode!

12
00:00:23,093 --> 00:00:25,600
Between the star and your eye, there is air.

13
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:29,726
And the air isn't calm: pockets of warm and cold air move all the time,

14
00:00:29,776 --> 00:00:31,403
like above a road in summer.

15
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:34,608
And each pocket bends the light a little.

16
00:00:34,658 --> 00:00:37,448
The star is so far away that it's just a point:

17
00:00:37,498 --> 00:00:40,409
its tiny ray jumps right, left, brighter, dimmer…

18
00:00:40,459 --> 00:00:41,184
it twinkles!

19
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:43,489
But the planet, closer to us,

20
00:00:43,539 --> 00:00:45,079
is a small disk, not a point.

21
00:00:45,129 --> 00:00:47,710
Its rays pass through lots of different pockets,

22
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:49,245
so the jumps blend together…

23
00:00:49,295 --> 00:00:50,774
and its light stays steady.

24
00:00:51,554 --> 00:00:53,159
And up there, above the air?

25
00:00:53,209 --> 00:00:56,587
Nothing trembles anymore, the stars shine perfectly still…

26
00:00:56,637 --> 00:00:59,060
that's why we send telescopes into space!

27
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:02,023
And that's why stars twinkle.

28
00:01:03,348 --> 00:01:04,596
Stars shine steadily;

29
00:01:04,646 --> 00:01:08,231
it's the moving air above us that makes their light dance.

30
00:01:09,834 --> 00:01:11,419
With an adult, in the dark:

31
00:01:11,469 --> 00:01:14,627
shine a light on the ceiling through a bowl of water.

32
00:01:14,677 --> 00:01:17,351
Stir the water, and the spot of light dances,

33
00:01:17,401 --> 00:01:18,128
like a star!

34
00:01:18,904 --> 00:01:20,939
And what is a shooting star?

35
00:01:20,989 --> 00:01:22,479
The answer tomorrow.
